    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTE142/technical-services-manager": {
      "title": "Technical Services Manager",
      "description": "Technical Services Manager at University of Warwick This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Technical Services Manager University of Warwick - WMS - Biomedical Sciences Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £47,389 to £56,535\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 6th October 2026 Closes: 20th October 2026 Job Ref: 369 Closing Date: Tuesday, 20 October 2026, 11:59pm (UK). About the Role This is a unique opportunity to join Warwick Biomedical Sciences as its Technical Services Manager, leading the Biomedical Sciences Technical Support function that works across 2 sites - one at Gibbet Hill Campus and the other at the Clinical Sciences Research Laboratories at UHCW. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description. Informal enquiries are welcome. Please contact recruiting manager, Catherine Newman, Head of Operations via Catherine.Newman@warwick.ac.uk . For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description ( link here ). About You You will be an experienced technical services leader with a strong track record of managing laboratory-based teams, specialist facilities and scientific infrastructure within a complex research or higher education environment. You will combine sound knowledge of laboratory health and safety, statutory compliance and governance with the ability to plan strategically, manage budgets and competing priorities, and deliver practical improvements to services, systems and equipment. A collaborative and credible communicator, you will be confident working with staff, students, senior leaders, professional services and external partners, while developing people, supporting change and fostering a positive, inclusive and safety-focused culture. About the Department Warwick Medical School has an excellent reputation for our distinctive portfolio of high-quality education programmes and for the excellence and global impact of our research. The breadth of our interest and expertise is demonstrated through our dynamic and influential directorates: Warwick Applied Health (WAH), Warwick Clinical Trials Unit (WCTU), and Warwick Biomedical Sciences (BMS). Our Institute of Translational Medicine (ITM) works across the directorates, University and with external stakeholders to accelerate the delivery of practical human health benefits arising from research. Warwick Biomedical Science’s mission is to advance world-class discovery science with an interdisciplinary approach to unravel the fundamental mechanisms of physiological and pathological processes; develop pioneering diagnostic and preventative technologies; and deliver ground-breaking treatments for a healthier future for all. Our research is grouped into the following disciplines: Cell and Mechano-Biology Discovery research with a focus on cytoskeletal self-organisation, membrane dynamics and tissue mechanobiology. Investigators in this theme form the core of the University-wide Centre for Mechanochemical Cell Biology. Host-Pathogen Interactions Discovery research and innovation focussing on pathogenicity factors and host machinery involved in infection and new approaches in diagnosis, prevention and immunity. Reproductive Biomedicine Discovery, translational and clinical research into gametogenesis, implantation, miscarriage, endometriosis, labour and birth with investigators forming the core of the Centre for Early Life and cross-cutting WMS programme in Women’s Health. For further information on the department, please see here . Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Programme Manager in AI for Infectious Diseases Store and Autoclave Technician (840399) Core Facilities Technician (Teaching and Research) Clinical Skills Tutor Senior Faculty Technician Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
