    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTD139/digital-communications-executive-content": {
      "title": "Digital Communications Executive (Content)",
      "description": "Digital Communications Executive (Content) at University of Warwick This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Digital Communications Executive (Content) University of Warwick - CCMOG - Brand, Campaigns and Marketing Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £31,236 to £34,610\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 1st October 2026 Closes: 15th October 2026 Job Ref: 333 About the Role We're looking for a creative and digitally-savvy content creator to join the commercial marketing team at the University of Warwick. This is an exciting opportunity for someone who loves creating engaging social media and digital content that captures attention, tells compelling stories and helps grow audiences. Working across a diverse portfolio of businesses including Warwick Sport, Warwick Conferences, Warwick Arts Centre, Warwick Food Group and the Innovation Group, you'll create content that supports marketing campaigns, customer engagement and commercial objectives. You'll be responsible for producing a wide range of content, with a particular focus on social media and video. From planning and filming short-form video content to  capturing events and creating engaging digital assets, you'll help bring our brands to life across multiple channels. No two days are the same. One day you might be filming content at a sporting event, the next creating social media assets for a cinema sales activation campaign, supporting a photoshoot or developing content ideas with colleagues across the University. This role is ideal for someone who combines creativity with strong organisational skills and enjoys working across multiple projects in a fast-paced environment . For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description ( link here ). About You You'll have experience producing engaging content for social media and digital channels, including photography, video and written content. You'll understand what works across different platforms and be comfortable managing the content creation process from idea through to delivery. We're looking for someone who: Has experience creating content for social media and digital channels Can shoot and edit high-quality photography and video content Has strong storytelling and copywriting skills Understands current social media trends and audience behaviours About the Department The University of Warwick is world leading for teaching and research, with an absolute commitment to excellence and an ambition to challenge the status quo. We’ve inspired positive change, sparked innovation, and created opportunity across our local community, our region, the country and beyond. We’re incredibly proud of our global reputation as a centre of excellence for learning and research. It is our mission to open our doors even wider – to work hand in hand with industry, to connect with academics and partners around the world, to bring opportunity to our region and our country, and to engage students, staff, and communities from all walks of life, all parts of society, all cultural backgrounds. You will join a passionate and inspiring team of Marketing, Communications, and Insight (MCI) professionals. MCI encompasses the teams for: Marketing and Student Recruitment. Brand and Marketing. Corporate Communications. Market Research and Insight. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Museum Education and Outreach Coordinator (Part Time, Fixed Term) Communications Officer (Students and Staff) Social Media Content Manager Engaged Research and Impact Manager Master Student Experience Coordinator Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
