    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTD756/electrical-services-officer": {
      "title": "Electrical Services Officer",
      "description": "Electrical Services Officer at University of Warwick This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Electrical Services Officer University of Warwick - Estates - Maintenance Operations - Electrical Services Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £35,608 to £46,049\n                                                                                        per annum. Hours: Full Time, Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 5th October 2026 Closes: 19th October 2026 Job Ref: 214 Closing Date: Monday, 19 October 2026, 11:59 pm. About the Role This is a re-advertisement, previous candidates need not apply. We will consider applications for employment on a part-time or other flexible working basis (e.g. job share), despite the position being advertised as full-time. The University of Warwick is seeking an experienced and motivated Electrical Services Officer (Fire & Security Systems) to play a vital role in maintaining the safety, compliance, and reliability of our extensive campus infrastructure. This is an excellent opportunity for a qualified electrical professional with experience in fire and security systems who is looking to take the next step in their career within a dynamic and supportive environment. As Electrical Services Officer, you will be responsible for overseeing the maintenance, compliance, and operational performance of the University's fire and security systems across campus. Working within the Maintenance Department, you will lead the delivery of planned preventative maintenance (PPM), inspections, testing programmes, remedial works, and installations carried out by both in-house teams and specialist contractors. You will ensure all activities are completed safely, efficiently, and in full compliance with statutory requirements, University policies, and industry standards. A key part of the role will involve providing technical leadership, maintaining accurate compliance records, and supporting the continuous improvement of services. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description (link here) . About You To be successful in this role, you will: Be a fully qualified electrician with substantial experience working on fire and security systems. Have previous supervisory or team leadership experience within a maintenance or facilities environment. Possess a strong understanding of statutory compliance requirements and industry best practice. Be highly organised, with excellent attention to detail and record-keeping skills. Demonstrate strong problem-solving abilities and the confidence to make informed technical decisions. Be an effective communicator who can build positive working relationships with colleagues, contractors, and stakeholders. Take a proactive and professional approach to delivering safe, reliable, and compliant services. About the Department Why Join the University of Warwick? At Warwick, you'll become part of a forward-thinking institution renowned for excellence, innovation, and collaboration. We value the expertise and commitment of our staff and provide an environment where you can develop and thrive. In return, we offer: Competitive salary of up to £46,049 per annum. 42 days annual leave (including bank holidays and customary days) . Generous pension scheme. Extensive staff benefits and wellbeing support. Opportunities for ongoing training and professional development. A supportive and inclusive working environment. The opportunity to contribute to one of the UK's leading university campuses. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this MEP Operations Manager Cleaner Porter Sustainability Behaviour Change & Engagement Officer Housekeeping Porter Facilities Officer Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
