    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTE584/programmes-administrator": {
      "title": "Programmes Administrator",
      "description": "Programmes Administrator at University of Warwick This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Programmes Administrator University of Warwick - Department of Computer Science Location: Coventry, University of Warwick, Hybrid Salary: £36,320 to £46,970\n                                                                                        per annum. Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 7th October 2026 Closes: 21st October 2026 Job Ref: 374 Closing Date: Wednesday, 21 October 2026, 11:59 pm (UK). About the Role The role-holder will lead the Student Support team to deliver for our student and staff community across a range of programme administration tasks with key responsibilities including coursework management, examinations and timetabling. You will be joining a team of friendly professionals who are committed to improving student experience at Warwick in our recently refurbished Student Support Office. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description ( link here ). About You The successful candidate will have strong organisational skills with the ability to work quickly and accurately under pressure. They will have excellent interpersonal skills to provide line management to a team of three direct reports. You will have a desire to continuously improve the student provision and will be enthusiastic about the opportunity to be involved in the development and implementation of new communication initiatives to reach our diverse student cohorts. Hybrid working is available (but not required) for two days per week, subject to business need. About the Department The Department of Computer Science is proud of their diverse community of staff, students and visitors, and are committed to maintaining an excellent record in teaching and research by ensuring there is equality of opportunity for all, fostered in an environment of mutual respect and dignity. The Department of Computer Science holds an Athena Swan - Silver Award. The award recognises advancement of gender equality: representation, progression and success for all. For further information about The Department of Computer Science, please visit our website: https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/ . How to Apply To apply please complete your essential personal details and attach a CV and cover letter on the closing date stated. Please ensure your CV includes your most recent employment experience along with any additional relevant experience and education history. Your cover letter should detail your motivation for applying for the role as well as detailing how you meet the essential and desirable criteria. Interview Date: To Be Confirmed. We will review applications throughout the advertising period and may contact shortlisted candidates before the closing date. We therefore encourage interested applicants to submit their application as early as possible. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early should we receive a sufficient number of suitable applications. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Timetable Officer School Education and Quality Manager Accounts Assistant Helpdesk Programme Coordinator, Professional Programmes Research Project Administrator Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended