    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSY821/student-records-senior-assistant": {
      "title": "Student Records - Senior Assistant",
      "description": "Student Records - Senior Assistant at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Student Records - Senior Assistant University of Warwick - Education - Operations Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £26,707 to £30,378\n                                                                                        per annum. Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 17th September 2026 Closes: 15th October 2026 Job Ref: 291 Closing Date: Thursday, 15 October 2026, 11:59PM. About the Role Candidates choosing this role will be joining one of the UK's leading universities, consistently ranked within the UK's top 10 and recognised globally for excellence in teaching, research, and student experience. Warwick is a dynamic, innovative institution with a strong reputation for student employability, a Gold-rated Teaching Excellence Framework award, and a diverse international community, providing opportunities to support students from a wide range of backgrounds and cultures. As part of the Student Records team, the successful candidate will play a key role in delivering services that directly support the University's reputation for excellence, while benefiting from a culture that values collaboration, continuous improvement, and professional development. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description (link here) . About You The successful candidate will be an organised, proactive, and customer-focused professional with excellent attention to detail and a commitment to delivering a high-quality service. They will be confident managing complex administrative processes, interpreting and applying regulations accurately, and working with sensitive data in a professional and confidential manner. Strong communication and interpersonal skills are essential, as the role involves building effective working relationships with students, academic departments, and professional services colleagues. The ideal candidate will be able to prioritise competing demands, demonstrate sound judgement when resolving queries, and contribute positively to service improvements, while embracing the collaborative, inclusive, and student-centred values of the University of Warwick. About the Department Education Operations is a newly established Directorate bringing together teams from Education Policy and Quality, Student Administrative Services, and Student Complaints and Academic Casework into a more connected and integrated professional services function. Our focus is on supporting excellent education delivery across the University by reducing complexity, improving consistency, strengthening governance and creating more seamless experiences for students and staff. We work across the academic lifecycle, from curriculum and assessment through to student records, casework, quality assurance and academic governance. The Directorate is being designed around end-to-end services, user-centred design, continuous improvement and smarter use of data and systems. This creates a unique opportunity for colleagues to help shape new approaches, influence institutional strategy and contribute to major change programmes at one of the UK’s leading universities. How to Apply To apply please complete your essential personal details and attach a CV and cover letter by the closing date and time stated. We will review applications throughout the advertising period and may contact shortlisted candidates before the closing date. We therefore encourage interested applicants to submit their application as early as possible. We reserve the right to close this vacancy early should we receive a sufficient number of suitable applications. Please ensure your CV includes your most recent employment experience along with any additional relevant experience and education history. Your cover letter should detail your motivation for applying for the role as well as detailing how you meet the essential and desirable criteria. The interviews will be held on a date to be confirmed. Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be cr