    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DTC646/administrative-coordinator": {
      "title": "Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Administrative Coordinator at University of Warwick Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Administrative Coordinator University of Warwick - School of Engineering Location: Coventry, University of Warwick Salary: £31,236 to £34,610\n                                                                                        per annum Hours: Full Time, Part Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 30th September 2026 Closes: 14th October 2026 Job Ref: 364 About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Caroline Whitehouse (Operations Manager) at c.whitehouse.1@warwick.ac.uk . Flexible Working We will consider applications for employment on a part-time or other flexible working basis (e.g. job share), despite the position being advertised as full-time. We welcome applications from candidates seeking a minimum of 29.2 hours per week (0.8 FTE). The School of Engineering is seeking an additional Administrative Coordinator to join the Staff Administration Team. This is a newly created role, reflecting the team’s need to deliver increasingly complex, cross functional work across the School. You will be leading on a broad range of People related administration across the employee lifecycle: from recruitment through to midlife processes (e.g.: academic progression, staff reward and performance schemes) through to leaving. You will be expected to become an expert in these cycles; navigating the University’s processes and policies to effectively deliver People related administration, plus guide and advise colleagues, including senior leaders, to enable them to do the same. Alongside recruitment activity, you will be sharing in the planning, implementation and evaluation of the annual cycle of staff administration support. This includes work that has a more project based element (e.g.: Graduate Teaching, Workload Model). We would also look to you to support other professional services staff teams within the School at busy times or to cover colleague absence. Much of the team’s work is shaped by the needs of senior managers, Academics and the School’s Executive Team. You’ll need to alleviate their pressure by working autonomously, using your knowledge, influence and confidence to guide them, anticipate requirements and make appropriate decisions. You won’t be unsupported though; this role is managed by the Operations Manager, works closely alongside another Administrative Coordinator, and is assisted by an Administrative Assistant(s) who’ll you line manage and develop. The role also offers the chance to contribute beyond the immediate team. You’ll help build and contribute to informal networks of colleagues in similar roles in the eight departments that form the Science and Engineering (S&E) hub. These networks are being established to share good practice (including with colleagues from central professional service areas, e.g. People), with the aim of developing more consistent approaches and processes across departments in the S&E hub. Your contribution to supporting and championing this approach, and offering support to other departments in the S&E hub on an occasional basis, will be key to its development and success. With distinct areas of ownership, and a wide remit, this is an impactful role that offers a great opportunity to take your first step into line management, and have a taste of project based work. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description ( link here ) . Full details of the duties and selection criteria for this role can be found in the vacancy advert on the University of Warwick's jobs pages. You will be routed to this when you click on the 'Apply' button. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Ok Ok PhD Alert Created Job Alert Created Your PhD alert has been successfully created for this search. Your job alert has been successfully created for this search. Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Account Verification Missing In order to create multiple job alerts, you must first verify your email address to complete your account creation Request verification email Request verification email jobs.ac.uk Account Required In order to create multiple alerts, you must create a jobs.ac.uk jobseeker account Create Account Create Account Alert Creation Failed Unfortunately, your account is currently blocked. Please login to unblock your account. Login Login Email Address Blocked We received a delivery failure message when attempting to send you an email and therefore your email address has been blocked. You will not receive job alerts until your email address is unblocked. To do so, please choose from one of the two options below. Re-verify your email Update your email Re-verify your email Update your email Max Alerts Reached A maximum of 5 Job Alerts can be created against your account. Please remove an existing alert in order to create this new Job Alert Manage your job alerts Manage your job alerts Creation Failed Unfortunately, your alert was not created at this time. Please try again. Ok Ok Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you create this PhD alert we will email you a selection of PhDs matching your criteria. When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy apply to this service. Any personal data you provide in setting up this alert is processed in accordance with our Privacy Notice Create PhD Alert Create Job Alert When you create this PhD alert we will email you a selection of PhDs matching your criteria. When you create this job alert we will email you a selection of jobs matching your criteria. Our Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy apply to this service. Any personal data you provide in setting up this alert is processed in accordance with our Privacy Notice I would like to receive email communication from jobs.ac.uk relating to Company News I would like to receive email communication from jobs.ac.uk relating to Conferences, Meetings and Events Save this job Login to Save Job Max Saved Jobs Reached × Max Saved Jobs Reached A maximum of 500 Saved Jobs can be created against your account. Please remove an existing Saved Job in order to add a new Saved Job. Manage Saved Jobs × Save Job Please sign in or register for an account to save a job. Sign In Register More jobs from University of Warwick Early Years Practitioner (Nursery Assistant) Mechanical Maintenance Manager Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager Associate Professor (Human-AI Teaming) Research Fellow Assistant Clinical Professor Show all jobs for this employer … More jobs like this Timetable Officer School Education and Quality Manager Accounts Assistant Helpdesk Programme Coordinator, Professional Programmes Research Project Administrator Join in and follow us Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
